  "scope": "Early prebuild bound on new SDS 4-inch, NEO drive and NEO azimuth. Preserves registered centerline, six rest-to-rest azimuth changes, 20 ms transition latency each, 250 ms dock settle and a 3.5 s stationary pre-tip window. Differential profile class controls the center position and yaw only. Does not certify tracking, thermal capacity, DC braking energy acceptance, occupancy, 4-wheel traction distribution, sensed placement or source pan drive. Articulated inertia, pan speed limit, total mass/CG, scrub and wire resistance are provisional. Regeneration contributes zero available supply. All nine motors plus 68 W auxiliary concurrently budgeted as a sufficient envelope, not an observation. Weak pack, loaded tire radius, path/clock, achievable steering and current limits can reopen the ratios."
